PATCH 332: reconstruct MGAVIDEO mga FUN_0000_2004 (cockpit-instrument sprite BOUNDING-BOX analyzer, asm
0x2004-0x21d5) + its finalizer FUN_0000_21d6 (asm 0x21d6-0x22be).  2004 scans the loaded instrument sheet
(container.word0) row-by-row for the sprite key byte, tracks min/max X,Y, and writes the bbox into the
child view record at [+4]=minY [+6]=minX [+8]=maxY+1 [+0xa]=maxX [+0x14]=parity -- the fields
FUN_0000_2322 reads to populate the reticle geometry DGROUP:0x156c (width=maxX-minX, height=(maxY+1-minY)).
Both were Ghidra WRECKS (the two [DGROUP:0xcc] device-allocs arg-dropped to NULL scratch, the [0x336] row
unpacker mis-called as a near mga vector, all segment bases lost onto host NULL, the repnz/repz scas
run-scan + the RLE compaction on NULL pointers).  Reconstructed faithfully vs re_out/fist_mga_image.bin:
  - [0xcc] device-alloc resolved to the engine allocator FUN_1000_182a directly (uninstalled vector,
    patch-049 class): alloc1 0xc00 -> word[child] (child.word0 = the compiled-sprite buffer, part (e)),
    alloc2 0x140 -> word[0x1590] (per-row scratch);
  - [0x336] = 0xf69:0x57cb PackBits row unpacker reconstructed inline (patch-093 idiom, di+cx terminator);
  - DS=word[child] (buf1), ES=word[0x1590] (buf2), sheet=word[container]; scas run-scan + min/max bbox +
    the 0x2110-0x2136 even-rounding/parity, then the 0x2139-0x21a5 buf1 column re-encode;
  - 21d6 rebased onto buf1seg with WORD stride (pristine logic 1:1; Ghidra had it on host-NULL uint* 4B);
    the trailing [0xd4] realloc is an uninstalled no-op (buffer just not shrunk -- harmless).
The bbox locals are FINAL at asm 0x2136 (the re-encode + 21d6 only build the drawable sprite, bounded to
buf1's segment -> crash-free even if imperfect; no mission-cockpit pixel reference exists).  Paired with
patch 331 (which stops 1963 from zeroing DGROUP:0x68c=mga:0x2004) and patch 333 (which threads the c68c
args) -> the reticle geometry populates 288x81.  Mission-path only -> behaviour-neutral for the 24 flows.

